{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"e3eb6d12aba0c301d32b278bf9bdd6f98155308f","body":"Add complete public-consumer coverage for a delivery paid in two installments across separate approval and receipt conditions. The tests compare the entire parsed Program and filled Plan, four library reports, and four real CLI JSON/stdout results against frozen expectations. They feed each actual continuation into the next call, verify that the partial duty remains at the second condition, preserve that continuation on a false observation, and retain the fully discharged duty as present-zero.\n\nLocal validation: **3 passed, 0 failed, 0 filtered**, in **52.898060 seconds** including the cold build, with `mori --no-default-features`. The independent 34-member expectation packet was frozen before execution. The tested source is `078047940fb76e1ef62842f45dadd41a6592f99a` / tree `1639828b943114f96fefe5861dae18b9abca44b7`. A fresh exact formatted-source, actual-result and guarded-integration audit approved this result. The earlier source approval remains scoped to the original unformatted bytes.\n\nThe fixtures record declared public source/DTO visibility and incidental helper exposure. One normative source excerpt retains its immutable blank EOF line under an exact hash custody record. These checks exercise the existing local staged interpreter; there is no production semantic change, authentication, proof or ledger settlement claim. All fourteen staged gaps and original language/financial/target exits remain open.\n","files":[{"path":"crates/fixtures/core2-partial-delivery-complete/CASES.json","additions":66,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"crates/fixtures/core2-partial-delivery-complete/DERIVATION.md","additions":149,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"crates/fixtures/core2-partial-delivery-complete/FINANCIAL-AND-WORK.json","additions":800,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"crates/fixtures/core2-partial-delivery-complete/FREEZE.sha256","additions":34,"